I am still sitting at my table in the living room in Copenhagen.
I write the last words in my diary.
Then I put my pen on the table.
I close the little book and smile.
It was an absolutely perfect weekend in Odense.
I think back on my good trip.
I remember the old man who painted his house.
I also remember the stressed father and his naughty dog on the train.
I laugh a little to myself.
I look out of my open window.
The evening is incredibly long and light.
The sun is slowly going down over the city.
It gets dark very slowly.
I love my first spring in Denmark.
Tomorrow a new week starts.
I have to get up early and take the bus to work.
But tonight I have plenty of time.
I stand up and walk out into the kitchen.
I fetch a glass of cold water.
I am ready for Monday.
